From: Marc Plano-Lesay <kernald@enoent.fr>
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: shorten the TX watchdog on PCIe-attached GEM

Commit e438ec3e9e95 ("net: macb: add TX stall timeout callback to recover
from lost TSTART write") recovers a stalled TX queue from ndo_tx_timeout.
macb does not set watchdog_timeo, so the netdev watchdog uses its 5 s
default, and each stall on a Raspberry Pi 5 stops TX for 5 to 6 s.

Set watchdog_timeo to 1 s on GEMs that have MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES,
which today means only RP1. Other macb users keep the default.

Link: https://github.com/yama6a/talos-raspberry-pi5/issues/56
Signed-off-by: Marc Plano-Lesay <kernald@enoent.fr>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
@@ -4971,6 +4971,13 @@

 	dev->netdev_ops = &macb_netdev_ops;

+	/* A PCIe-attached GEM can lose a TSTART write and stall its TX queue.
+	 * ndo_tx_timeout recovers the queue, so shorten the netdev watchdog
+	 * from the 5 s default to recover sooner.
+	 */
+	if (bp->caps & MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES)
+		dev->watchdog_timeo = HZ;
+
 	/* setup appropriated routines according to adapter type */
 	if (macb_is_gem(bp)) {
 		bp->macbgem_ops.mog_alloc_rx_buffers = gem_alloc_rx_buffers;
